.TH TAIA_NOW 1 "April 2026" "go-libtai" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taia_now \- display current TAIA64 time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taia_now
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B taia_now
prints the current TAIA64 time, which includes nanosecond precision.
The output shows the time in seconds with fractional precision and as 
an external TAI64N format.
.PP
The TAI64N format consists of the TAI64 seconds (8 bytes) followed by 
the nanoseconds (4 bytes), represented in hexadecimal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tai_now (1),
.BR tai64n (1)
.SH AUTHOR
This tool is part of go-libtai, a Go implementation of D. J. Bernstein's 
libtai.
.SH NOTES
The TAIA64 format and its specifications were originally established by 
D. J. Bernstein in his libtai library (https://cr.yp.to/libtai.html).
